<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūtrīcŭla</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		dim.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				nurse</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid voveat dulci nutricula majus alumno?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 4, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 94</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fabulae nutricularum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					1, 9, 2</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>she who nourishes,
				maintains, preserves</i> a thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nutriculae praediorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 11, 5, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gellius nutricula seditiosorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Vatin. 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nutricula causidicorum Africa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					7, 148</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">casa nutricula,</span>”
				<i>in which one was brought up</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. Decl. 13, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
